{"availability":"available","full":"tikv/tikv","name":"tikv","description":"Distributed transactional key-value database, originally created to complement TiDB","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":16905,"forks":2357,"created":"2015-12-31T04:51:32Z","updated":"2026-10-05T05:24:11Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://tikv.org","topics":["cncf","consensus","distributed-transactions","hacktoberfest","key-value","raft","rocksdb","rust","tidb","tikv"],"demo":"https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/stable/quick-start-with-tidb#deploy-a-local-test-environment-using-tiup-playground","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:06:01.806Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T21:06:01.806Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T21:06:01.806Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:38:23.845Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:53.779Z","stars":16901,"forks":2355},{"at":"2026-10-04T19:21:02.392Z","stars":16903,"forks":2356},{"at":"2026-10-06T21:06:01.806Z","stars":16905,"forks":2357}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["TiKV is an open-source, distributed, and transactional key-value database. Unlike other traditional NoSQL systems, TiKV not only provides classical key-value APIs, but also transactional APIs with ACID compliance. Built in Rust and powered by Raft, TiKV was originally created by PingCAP to complement TiDB, a distributed HTAP database compatible with the MySQL protocol.","The design of TiKV ('Ti' stands for titanium) is inspired by some great distributed systems from Google, such as BigTable, Spanner, and Percolator, and some of the latest achievements in academia in recent years, such as the Raft consensus algorithm.","TiKV is a graduated project of the Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF). If you are an organization that wants to help shape the evolution of technologies that are container-packaged, dynamically-scheduled and microservices-oriented, consider joining the CNCF. For details about who's involved and how TiKV plays a role, read the CNCF announcement."],"features":["Horizontal scalability","Consistent distributed transactions","Cooperates with TiDB"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tikv/tikv/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"58a21aba3c4496806139219d5f61ad2ad1ae44ecfec555812c9d1c371489a450","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:00:17.502Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T21:09:43.591Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T05:24:11Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T16:40:12.038Z","latestRelease":{"name":"TiKV v7.5.8","tag":"v7.5.8","publishedAt":"2026-09-17T05:57:47Z","url":"https://github.com/tikv/tikv/releases/tag/v7.5.8"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:40:12.038Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/2dc6f7e0927b05e22c736ab6.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:12.724Z","url":"https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/stable/quick-start-with-tidb#deploy-a-local-test-environment-using-tiup-playground"}],"demoHealth":{"url":"https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/stable/quick-start-with-tidb#deploy-a-local-test-environment-using-tiup-playground","attemptedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:12.724Z","status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:12.724Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-06T21:13:12.724Z","target":"https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/stable/quick-start-with-tidb/#deploy-a-local-test-environment-using-tiup-playground","failureCount":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-13T21:13:12.724Z","probeVersion":3,"consecutiveTemporaryFailures":0},"projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"TiKV is an open-source, distributed, and transactional key-value database. Unlike other traditional NoSQL systems, TiKV not only provides classical key-value APIs, but also transactional APIs with ACID compliance. Built in Rust and powered by Raft, TiKV was originally created by PingCAP to complement TiDB, a distributed HTAP database compatible with the MySQL protocol.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tikv/tikv/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"58a2